  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, says a man named Joseph McMoneagle was given the Legion of Merit, a US military award, for remote viewing, which means trying to see distant places or hidden things using only the mind. According to Michels, McMoneagle used it more than 200 times to help gather intelligence, working on hostage cases and drawing nuclear sites. If true, it would mean the military found mind-based spying useful enough to reward it."
